se provenance when a +1 reopens a bead[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A bead that was closed and later reopened keeps the reason it was [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]closed, and every surface that shows the bead says plainly that it [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]was previously closed, why, and what reopened it — including which [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]+1 did it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bead_close_history.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/bead_close_history.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-fr[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-fr/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable close history in the bead event reducer[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-model: add BeadCloseRecordWire and IssueWire.close_history to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core, archive close metadata instead of discarding it on every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reopen path, unify the mutation and reducer paths on one helper, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the release and carry close history through Python [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]storage[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-adopt: raise the sase-core-rs window to the release from core-model[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and thread close_history through the Python model, wire conversion, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]issues.jsonl, the SQLite mirror with its migration, and the projection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repair guard.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared reopen presentation vocabulary[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]presentation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation: add sase/bead/reopen_presentation.py with the accent, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph, section label, badge, record labels, search text, and the single [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared join that decides which +1 entry reopened a bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase bead show, JSON, list badges, and search[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: render the PREVIOUSLY CLOSED section and the reopening-+1 marker in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead detail, emit close_history in detail JSON, add the reopen badge to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list/ready/search rows, and make archived close reasons searchable.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prior-close warning in the TaskTriage gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]triage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage: put a prior-close callout above the description in the task [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage preview, mark the reopening +1, add the reopen badge to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notification note, and include close history in the chop's presentation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fingerprint.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE beads pane close history[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]ace[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace: show the reopen badge on beads list rows, a Previously closed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]property and body section in the detail pane, and a has:reopened filter,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with PNG snapshot coverage.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generated bead pages close history[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pages[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pages: render a Previously Closed section and primary-fact badge on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]generated bead pages and add a reopen column to the lineage roster.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document close history and reopen provenance[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli, triage, ace, pages[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: document the close-history record, the reopen causes, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retroactive recovery from the event log, and every surface that renders [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]it in docs/beads.md.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-fr","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-fr.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-3ad00f36a2c5a4cd9494176e248dda49","started_at":"2026-08-06T01:32:18.863813+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785983714,"sha":"1da5a3e277326bf52cf79c72c1ec824cbdc2e02b","subject":"feat(bead): carry close history through Python bead storage"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"440bca6f977bf014d1d527c899c53